                <div><p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">History taking and treatment planning</p><p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">The psychologist understands your trauma history and identifies target memories.</p></div>
              </div>
              <div class="flex gap-4 bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary text-white text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">2</span>
                <div><p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Preparation</p><p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Safe-place exercises and an explanation of how EMDR works.</p></div>
              </div>
              <div class="flex gap-4 bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary text-white text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">3</span>
                <div><p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Assessment</p><p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Target memory, negative belief, emotions and body sensations are identified.</p></div>
